7. OUTCOME DEFINITIONS AND CLASSIFICATIONS

7.1 Comprehensive Outcome List

Our analysis included 49 maternal and fetal pregnancy outcomes classified into the following categories:

7.1.1 Fertility and Early Pregnancy (5 outcomes)
- Female infertility: ICD-10 N97 (FinnGen)
- Ectopic pregnancy: ICD-10 O00 (FinnGen)
- Miscarriage (subsample): Pregnancy loss <20 weeks (MR-PREG)
- Single miscarriage (subsample): One pregnancy loss episode (MR-PREG)
- Recurrent miscarriage (subsample): ≥2 consecutive losses (MR-PREG)

7.1.2 Placental Disorders (3 outcomes)
- Placenta praevia: ICD-10 O44 (FinnGen)
- Placental abruption: ICD-10 O45 (FinnGen)
- Other placental disorders: ICD-10 O43 (FinnGen)

7.1.3 Hypertensive Disorders (3 outcomes)
- Preeclampsia (subsample): Hypertension with proteinuria ≥20 weeks (MR-PREG)
- Gestational hypertension (subsample): Hypertension without proteinuria (MR-PREG)
- Hypertensive disorders (subsample): Combined preeclampsia and gestational hypertension (MR-PREG)

7.1.4 Metabolic and Other Medical Complications (3 outcomes)
- Gestational diabetes (subsample): Glucose intolerance during pregnancy (MR-PREG)
- Anaemia in pregnancy: Hemoglobin <11 g/dL (MR-PREG)
- Hyperemesis gravidarum: Severe nausea and vomiting requiring medical intervention (MR-PREG)

7.1.5 Preterm Birth and Membrane Rupture (4 outcomes)
- Preterm birth (all): Delivery <37 weeks gestation (MR-PREG)
- Preterm birth (subsample): Subset analysis <37 weeks (MR-PREG)
- Very preterm birth: Delivery <32 weeks gestation (MR-PREG)
- Premature rupture of membranes: Membrane rupture before labor onset (MR-PREG)

7.1.6 Delivery Mode and Labor (4 outcomes)
- Caesarean section (all): Any cesarean delivery (MR-PREG)
- Elective caesarean section: Planned cesarean before labor (MR-PREG)
- Emergency caesarean section: Unplanned cesarean during labor (MR-PREG)
- Induction of labour: Artificial initiation of labor (MR-PREG)

7.1.7 Fetal Growth and Birth Outcomes (6 outcomes)
- Low birthweight: <2,500 g (MR-PREG)
- High birthweight: >4,000 g (MR-PREG)
- Small for gestational age: <10th percentile for gestational age (MR-PREG)
- Large for gestational age: >90th percentile for gestational age (MR-PREG)
- Birthweight Z-score: Standardized birthweight adjusted for gestational age (MR-PREG)
- Post-term birth: Delivery ≥42 weeks gestation (MR-PREG)

7.1.8 Gestational Age Outcomes (2 outcomes)
- Gestational age (all): Continuous measure in days (MR-PREG)
- Gestational age (subsample): Subset analysis (MR-PREG)

7.1.9 Neonatal Outcomes (6 outcomes)
- Apgar score at 1 minute: Neonatal assessment score 0-10 (MR-PREG)
- Apgar score at 5 minutes: Neonatal assessment score 0-10 (MR-PREG)
- Low Apgar score at 1 minute: Score <7 at 1 minute (MR-PREG)
- Low Apgar score at 5 minutes: Score <7 at 5 minutes (MR-PREG)
- NICU admission: Neonatal intensive care unit admission (MR-PREG)
- Stillbirth (subsample): Fetal death ≥20 weeks gestation (MR-PREG)

7.1.10 Bleeding Complications (6 outcomes)
- Postpartum hemorrhage: Blood loss >500 mL vaginal or >1000 mL cesarean (Westergaard)
- PPH due to uterine atony: PPH caused by inadequate uterine contraction (Westergaard)
- PPH due to retained placenta: PPH caused by incomplete placental delivery (Westergaard)
- Antepartum bleeding: Bleeding during pregnancy ≥20 weeks (Westergaard)
- Early bleeding (any outcome): Bleeding <20 weeks, any pregnancy outcome (Westergaard)
- Early bleeding (live birth): Bleeding <20 weeks ending in live birth (Westergaard)

7.1.11 Maternal Mental Health and Other Outcomes (4 outcomes)
- Postpartum depression (subsample): Depression diagnosis within 1 year postpartum (MR-PREG)
- Severe nausea/vomiting (all): Clinically significant nausea/vomiting (MR-PREG)
- Severe nausea/vomiting (subsample): Subset analysis (MR-PREG)

7.1.12 Breastfeeding Outcomes (4 outcomes)
- Breastfeeding initiation: Any breastfeeding at birth (MR-PREG)
- Breastfeeding ≥4 months: Continued breastfeeding ≥4 months (MR-PREG)
- Exclusive breastfeeding: Exclusive breastfeeding at specified timepoint (MR-PREG)
- Breastfeeding cessation: Early cessation of breastfeeding (MR-PREG)

7.2 Sample Size Distribution

Sample sizes varied considerably across outcomes and data sources:

Largest samples (>500,000):
- Gestational diabetes (714,933)
- Hypertensive disorders (541,809)
- Preeclampsia (672,032)
- Preterm birth (512,086)

Moderate samples (100,000-500,000):
- Miscarriage (486,258)
- Hyperemesis gravidarum (478,503)
- Post-term birth (414,698)
- Recurrent miscarriage (321,790)
- Premature rupture of membranes (310,663)

Smaller samples (<100,000):
- Most neonatal outcomes (60,000-90,000)
- Breastfeeding outcomes (65,000-85,000)
- Delivery mode outcomes (87,000-234,000)

FinnGen and Westergaard outcomes had smaller but well-powered sample sizes focused on specific phenotypes with high-quality registry-based definitions.

