10. SUPPLEMENTARY TABLES

Supplementary Table S1. Complete List of 41 Genetic Instruments for Endometriosis

[THIS IS TABLE: A detailed table showing the 41 SNPs used as genetic instruments, including chromosomal position, effect allele, other allele, effect allele frequency, beta coefficient, standard error, p-value, and F-statistic for each variant. The data shows variants distributed across all chromosomes with strong instrument strength (all F > 38) and genome-wide significance (all P < 5×10⁻⁸).]

The 41 independent genetic variants collectively explain 5.6% of the variance in endometriosis liability with a mean F-statistic of 279.3, providing strong instrumental variable strength for Mendelian randomization analysis.

Sample sizes for endometriosis exposure data range from 199,170 to 206,106 participants across the different SNPs, reflecting the meta-analysis structure of the Rahmioglu et al. GWAS.

